  "summary": "An axial flow fan moves air parallel to its shaft. Aerofoil blades on a hub act like small wings: as they turn they push air along the casing. Outlet guide vanes remove the swirl the blades add, turning it into pressure. Axial fans give large flow at low-to-medium pressure and are used for ventilation, cooling towers, tunnels and (with variable-pitch blades) large boiler draft fans.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Fan (dynamic)",
    "type": "Vane-axial fan, direct drive, in-line motor"
  },
